        "detailed_analysis": "The pattern is a well-crystallized powder with ~17 resolved reflections between 5\u00b0 and 45\u00b0 2\u03b8. The global fit is essentially perfect (R\u00b2=0.99999); peak_region_r2=0.9993 comfortably exceeds the 0.90 acceptance gate. The residual/noise trace is structureless over the bulk of the pattern, with the only significant excursions being narrow dispersive features at the cores of the strongest peaks (11.9\u00b0, 17.5\u201318\u00b0, 20\u00b0). These are the classic apex misfit of a split pseudo-Voigt against a near-instrumental-width core carrying the highest counts; per the domain rules this is the irreducible profile limit and should be accepted rather than chased with symmetric sub-fits. Crystallite-size analysis: per-peak Scherrer values run 25\u201332 nm for the majority of reflections, placing the material in the typical microcrystalline regime (~25\u201332 nm). Two peaks (5.9\u00b0\u2192wait: peaks 5 at 17.9\u00b0 and 15 at 29.5\u00b0) sit lower at ~15\u201317 nm, and peak 1 at 5.1\u00b0 returns 7.5 nm but lies at the excluded low-angle edge where SNIP background contamination inflates the apparent width \u2014 it is discarded. Excluding that artifact, the per-peak spread is ~15\u201332 nm, a factor of ~2, below the >3\u00d7 anisotropy-flag threshold but large enough to note mild broadening variation (possible hkl-dependent/anisotropic broadening on a couple of reflections). The Williamson-Hall decomposition FAILS its sanity gate (R\u00b2=0.16 \u00ab0.7, slope negative \u2192 unphysical strain); by the mandatory rules the strain/size decomposition is NOT reported, and the negative slope is attributed to the mixed size spread / weak FWHM-vs-2\u03b8 trend rather than real compressive strain. Only a per-peak Scherrer size range is reported. Several eta values are pinned at 0 or 1, so those peaks are effectively pure Lorentzian/Gaussian by default and their shape (not their FWHM) is underconstrained. Because this is an in-situ dehydration ramp, peak positions and relative intensities are expected to evolve frame-to-frame; the auto-detecting global recipe is appropriate for tracking this. Reported crystallite domain size for this frame: approximately 25 nm (range ~15\u201332 nm across reflections), \u00b1~15% instrumental accuracy.",
